## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates understanding of multi-tenant GPU sharing in Kubernetes, MIG partition management, NVIDIA device plugin integration, and the ability to build custom resource controllers for quota enforcement with burst handling.

## Key Concepts

- GPU quota management in shared clusters
- MIG (Multi-Instance GPU) partitions
- CRD and controller patterns
- Resource enforcement via scheduler hints
- Observability for GPU workloads

## Code Example

```go
func (r *GPUQuotaReconciler) Reconcile(ctx context.Context, req ctrl.Request) (ctrl.Result, error) {
    ns := &corev1.Namespace{}
    if err := r.Get(ctx, req.NamespacedName, ns); err != nil {
        return ctrl.Result{}, client.IgnoreNotFound(err)
    }

    gpuQuota := &GPUQuota{}
    if err := r.Get(ctx, req.NamespacedName, gpuQuota); err != nil {
        return ctrl.Result{}, client.IgnoreNotFound(err)
    }

    available GPUs, err := r.getAvailableGPUs(ns.Name)
    if err != nil {
        return ctrl.Result{}, err
    }

    if gpuQuota.Spec.Burst.Enabled {
        if isWithinBurstWindow(gpuQuota) {
            return r.reconcileBurst(ctx, gpuQuota, availableGPUs)
        }
    }

    return r.enforceQuota(ctx, gpuQuota, availableGPUs)
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design a Kubernetes-native multi-tenant shard architecture, implement operator-driven lifecycle management, and construct safe upgrade and backup workflows—essential skills for building scalable platforms serving multiple customers.

## Key Concepts

- CustomResourceDefinition design and operator reconciliation loops
- StatefulSets with per-tenant PVCs and resource quotas
- Canary rollouts with per-tenant rate limiting
- Cross-tenant backup orchestration and disaster recovery
- PodDisruptionBudgets for controlling upgrade blast radius

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo reconciliation loop
async function reconcileTenantShard(cr) {
  const ns = cr.metadata.namespace;
  await ensureNamespace(ns);
  const sts = buildStatefulSet(cr);
  await applyStatefulSet(sts);
  const pdb = buildPodDisruptionBudget(cr);
  await applyPDB(pdb);
  const backupJob = buildBackupJob(cr);
  await scheduleBackup(backupJob);
  await updateStatus(cr, { phase: 'Ready' });
}
```
